# Prove two-host delivery recovery and publish operator documentation

## Context

Design: `.collab/design/2026-10-19-c2c-t3-external-connector.md`.
Pending planned work. During execution follow bl-fix-many: read the full ticket, verify blockers, commit the claim, work in an isolated worktree, review/fix, run the c2c gates on build boxes, merge and close. No T3 source changes. Tests use x-p35/x-tuf, never the workstation's full suite. Actual just bi and service installation wait for the current candidate's successful P9.M2.E1.T001 buildbox gate.

## Requirements

- Review all changes against the accepted design, fix actionable findings and rerun appropriate c2c checks on isolated build-box roots. No full tests on the workstation.
- Prove real idle and active delivery with generic agent attribution and the canonical reply recipe on x-p35 and x-tuf. Record actual source and installed binary hashes.
- Verify relay sends both directions with unique nonces and correct replies, duplicate prevention, service restart, T3 fixture restart, response loss, retirement, permission denial and repair.
- Prove local direct delivery both with relay disabled and configured/enabled, without routing bare aliases over the network. Cross-host cases use relay.c2c.im only after compatible publication support and explicit rollout. User confirmed no new direct cross-host transport is required.
- Update user docs to describe unmodified T3 and native c2c service, superseding C2cBridge as the setup path for this feature. Preserve historical research accurately.
- Produce a concise install/health/limitation receipt. A local commit or binary install does not authorize an origin push or relay deployment.
- Verify the integrated recovery monitor: current root availability failure, native-child and mixed-error negatives, in-place retry update, Stop marker/queued work, snooze/approval/connector holds, queue-mode concurrent-start race, one-second shared dispatch spacing, 60-second sweeps, restart/response-loss/re-pair dedupe and explicit disable. Use designated fixtures, never unrelated threads.
- Any source or generated-code fix invalidates the old buildbox receipt: repeat P9.M2.E1.T001 for that candidate before P9.M2.E1.T002 just bi/reinstallation. Document changes may use scoped validation only if they do not alter installed sources/generated artifacts, with source identity linked explicitly.

## Acceptance Criteria

- All required c2c just gates passed on the exact installed candidate before installation, with exact invocation/result recorded. An environmental limitation is a blocker, not a substituted PASS.
- Live evidence proves one delivery and expected attribution for both idle and active targets on actual installed builds, with no unrelated user threads changed.
- Service repair and retirement preserve pending mail and foreign state; full-access target denial and credential rotation uncertainty are visible.
- Documentation and shipped CLI agree. The backlog is closed only after reviewed implementation is merged and required validation completes.
- Recovery positive and negative external-API cases are demonstrated on supported hosts. Distinguish real model-outage reproduction from fixture-induced failure; report any unverified live-outage behavior explicitly.

## Lane

Final serial review/validation lane after all implementation. Coordinate isolated fixture threads and avoid restarting the user's live T3 services.


## Validation result 2026-10-20 — partial / external blocker

Local direct delivery passed on both x-tuf and x-p35 with agent/mcp attribution, DATA framing and canonical c2c reply footer. A temporary isolated relay built from the same candidate passed both directions with unique nonces and transcript delivery. Recovery fixture/unit coverage passed and live 401 provider-auth failures correctly did not trigger Continue; a real model-availability outage was not reproduced.

The configured production relay `https://relay.c2c.im` currently returns the older capability surface; the installed connector reports `relay lacks signed T3 peer-publication capability`, so service-owned T3 aliases cannot be made publicly routable there. This task remains blocked for the production cross-host proof until that relay is deployed with the signed T3 peer-publication endpoint. No public relay deployment was performed.

2026-10-22 audit decision: one serial worktree lane for connector/footer corrections and final validation (shared service and CLI files). Prior evidence is partial: x-p35 just test failed because docker compose was missing, so its generated PASS receipt and resulting installation do NOT satisfy the gate. Revalidate all installed sources before any further install. T003 also lacks the complete integrated live matrix; the public relay rollout is one blocker, not the sole remaining work. Master push is authorized and Railway deploys automatically; no manual deploy or credential is required. Verify shared-broker reply scope, remote sender host preservation, and supported T3 0.1.1 behavior before completing.

